{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"bConnectedVertices"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"source"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"B-connection here is path-based, as B-Visit computes it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is B-connected to ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or some hyperedge with ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" among its targets is entered along a path","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (it has a source, and all its sources are B-connected). So ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a hyperedge with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no sources never fires","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": no path enters it, and B-Visit scans only the forward stars of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached vertices. The recursive reading (“every source is B-connected”) would fire it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vacuously from any start; Gallo et al.’s visit and halp do not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a vertex.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n + m + p): one counter per hyperedge and one queue; one hash."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Every vertex B-connected to ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" included, in vertex-index order: Gallo et","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"al.‘s B-Visit (halp’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"b_visit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). A hyperedge fires once every one of its sources has been","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached, and then reaches all its targets. On a directed graph read as a hypergraph this is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reachability.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceList"]]},"metadata":{"title":"bConnectedVertices(from:)","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedHypergraphAlgorithms.swift#L318","fileName":"DirectedHypergraphAlgorithms.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP11HypergraphsE18bConnectedVertices4fromSay6VertexQzGAH_tF